B.F7=s(["Local data remains on the device while the user keeps the app and does not delete it. There is no automatic expiration date for local history. Ads and data processed by Google are retained under Google\u2019s policies and controls, not Dopa\u2019s local storage mechanisms.","To erase Dopa\u2019s local information, users can select Settings > Delete my data in the app. This removes the library and its PDF copies, task plan and progress, optional name, selected apps, usage and blocking histories, and time settings. The accessibility-service permission and other permissions managed by Android are not revoked automatically; they are managed in the device settings.","Deleting data within Dopa does not erase information already processed by Google Mobile Ads or backups Android created before deletion. Users should use the Google and Android controls linked in this policy to manage that information. Uninstalling the app also does not guarantee immediate deletion of backups managed by Android or advertising data managed by Google.","Dopa does not offer account creation. Therefore, it does not maintain developer-server accounts that need to be deleted."],t.s)
