B.G6=s(["Local data is stored in the app\u2019s private areas, protected by Android and its app-isolation controls. Dopa does not keep a copy on its own servers. Transmission associated with Google Mobile Ads is handled by Google\u2019s SDK; Google says it encrypts data collected by that SDK in transit. No storage or transmission method can guarantee absolute security, so users should also protect their device and Google Account."],t.s)
B.Gb=s(["Dopa may show Google Mobile Ads banners on Android. Banners are requested only in locations enabled by the app and after the configured usage-day threshold. The version described in this policy does not use interstitial or rewarded ads.","When ads are loaded or displayed, Google\u2019s SDK may automatically collect and share with Google data such as:"],t.s)
B.Gc=s(["Optional name or nickname: text entered by the user to personalize the experience. It is stored on the device and is not sent to the developer.","Available and selected apps: Android provides the names, icons, and package names of apps that can be launched. The list is shown so the user can choose which apps to protect. Dopa stores the selection, not a persistent copy of the entire inventory it queried.","Protection data: when the accessibility service is enabled, it receives window-change events and the associated package name to identify the app in the foreground. Dopa uses this information to count time in selected apps, show a pause when the allowance runs out, and store daily usage of protected apps locally.","Blocking history: for selected apps, Dopa may store the date and time of a block, challenge results, and whether the user chose to return to the blocked app. This history supports Dopa\u2019s progress screens.","Usage data for averages: if the user grants optional access to Android usage data, Dopa may query the foreground time of an app for recent full days to show averages. When the user confirms adding a protected app, its initial average may be stored on the device as a reference.","Plan and progress: enabled games, number and difficulty of tasks, completed tasks, rewards, and time balance.","Reading library: imported PDF files are copied to the app\u2019s private storage. Library details such as title, page count, current page, reading time, and related rewards are also stored. Dopa does not send these documents to the developer or Google Mobile Ads.","App preferences and state: language, theme, settings, tutorial steps, and a local usage-day counter used to determine when banner ads may be requested."],t.s)
B.dD=s([B.bT,B.bh,B.et,B.eu,B.hx],t.QP)
B.Gd=s(["Dopa does not have user accounts or its own server to which it sends the name chosen by the user, selected apps, protection history, tasks, PDF files, or reading progress. This information is processed and stored on the device to provide the app\u2019s features.","The exception is advertising: when an ad is requested, Dopa integrates Google\u2019s Google Mobile Ads SDK. That SDK may collect and send Google certain device, app-usage, and ad-interaction data to provide, measure, and protect the advertising service. Android backups enabled by the user may also apply, as explained below."],t.s)
